# gitops-{{ environment }}-{{ service_name }}

GitOps deployment manifest for `{{ service_name }}` in `{{ environment }}`, reconciled by
{% if gitops_engine == 'argocd' %}Argo CD{% else %}Flux{% endif %}.

Generated by repave blueprint `gitops-deployment-generic`.

## Usage

The manifest in `apps/release.yaml` deploys chart `{{ chart_name }}` version `{{ chart_version }}`
from `{{ chart_repo_url }}` into namespace `{{ target_namespace }}`.

Promote a new chart version by editing `chart_version` in `apps/release.yaml` and merging:

```bash
yamllint apps
```

{% if gitops_engine == 'argocd' -%}
Apply the Application to the cluster that hosts Argo CD:

```bash
kubectl apply -f apps/release.yaml
```

Check reconciliation:

```bash
argocd app get {{ service_name }}-{{ environment }}
```
{%- else -%}
Flux reconciles `apps/` through the cluster `Kustomization` that points at this repository:

```bash
flux get helmrelease {{ service_name }}-{{ environment }} -n {{ flux_source_namespace }}
```

The `HelmRepository` named `{{ flux_source_name }}` must already exist in
`{{ flux_source_namespace }}`.
{%- endif %}

## Sync policy

This repository uses **{{ sync_policy }}** sync.

{% if sync_policy == 'automated' -%}
The controller applies chart changes without waiting for a human, with prune and self-heal
declared explicitly. A merged version bump reaches the cluster on the next reconcile.
{%- else -%}
The controller waits for an operator to apply or promote. A merged version bump does not reach
the cluster until someone syncs it.
{%- endif %}

## Configuration

| Field | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Chart | `{{ chart_name }}` |
| Version | `{{ chart_version }}` |
| Repository | `{{ chart_repo_url }}` |
| Namespace | `{{ target_namespace }}` |
| Environment | `{{ environment }}` |

Chart versions must be exact. Floating references (`HEAD`, `latest`, ranges) fail the `opa`
gate — see `standards/gitops/deployment-standard.md`.

